  "reply_text": "Found one merge-blocking issue:\n\n**[P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`**\n`share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` parses as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, which effectively checks the **READ** bit instead of WRITE.\n\nConfirmed:\n- `{ mask: READ, locked: false }` → `canEdit()` returns **true**, granting viewers edit access.\n- `{ mask: WRITE, locked: false }` → returns **0**, denying a share with WRITE permission.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE)` or parenthesize `(share.mask & WRITE) === WRITE`. Add tests for an unlocked viewer being denied and a WRITE-only share being allowed—the current editor test has both bits, so it misses this.\n\nAll 6 existing tests pass. No other concrete issues found in the diff against `main`. No files changed.",
